{"results":[{"url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/transparency/","final_url":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/transparency/","title":"Transparency","description":"The White House Transparency Task Force was formed by President Trump to expose government weaponization, failed foreign policies, and election integrity.","language":"en","text":"# Government Transparency & Election Integrity\n\nThe American people have a right to know what their Government does in their name. Unfortunately, crucial information about topics like the weaponization of Government by past administrations, failed foreign policy adventures whose consequences continue to reverberate in world events today, and honest intelligence assessments of the integrity of our elections remain hidden from view in the bowels of the Federal bureaucracy. It is time to bring this information into the light.\n\n## How the Task Force works\n\n* #### A three-member Task Force\n\n  Created inside the White House to advise the President, through the Counsel to the President, on which documents to declassify and release.\n* #### Records within 7 days\n\n  The Chief of Staff and the heads of State, Treasury, War, Justice, HHS, Homeland Security, ODNI and the CIA must provide requested documents within 7 calendar days.\n* #### Decisions within 10 days\n\n  The Counsel to the President consults national security and intelligence leaders within 10 calendar days of a request. The Task Force runs through December 31, 2026.\n\nSearch records\n\n## Election Integrity\n\nWhat the Intelligence Community, FBI and Department of Homeland Security found about the security of America’s voting machines, voter data and voter rolls.\n\n## Government Transparency\n\nInvestigative files, memos and court records on how federal agencies were weaponized, including against the President, his team and elected officials.\n\nNo records match that search. Try a name, agency or codename, or clear the search to see every record.\n\n## The SAVE America Act\n\nThe Safeguard American Voter Eligibility Act would set two national requirements for federal elections, so that only eligible citizens register and only registered voters cast ballots.\n\nLearn about the SAVE America Act\n\n### Proof of citizenship\n\nDocumentary proof of U.S. citizenship to register to vote in federal elections.\n\n### Photo ID\n\nA valid photo ID to cast a ballot.\n\n## DOJ and DHS election enforcement\n\nThe Justice Department’s Civil Rights Division, working with the Department of Homeland Security, tracks enforcement actions nationwide under Executive Order 14248, including lawsuits against states that refuse to produce voter rolls and prosecutions for noncitizen voting.\n\nView the state-by-state map\n\nStay Informed\n\n## Get the next update.\n\nNew findings, new filings, and next steps in the effort to secure our elections, delivered to your inbox as they land.","author":null,"published_date":"2026-10-22T10:00:00+00:00","latency_ms":663.09113400348,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}